.TH "WEBTRANSPORTDATAGRAMDUPLEXSTREAM.CREATEWRITABLE" "3JS" "September 1, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
WebTransportDatagramDuplexStream.createWritable \-
WebTransportDatagramDuplexStream: createWritable() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]createWritable()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]WebTransportDatagramDuplexStream\f[R] interface returns a
\f[CR]WebTransportDatagramsWritable\f[R] instance that can be used to
write outgoing datagrams to the transport.
.PP
It should be used instead of the deprecated \f[CR]writable\f[R] property
where it is supported.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
createWritable()
createWritable(options)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]options\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
An object that may have the following properties:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]sendGroup\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A \f[CR]WebTransportSendGroup\f[R] that the returned stream\(cqs
datagrams should be grouped under for the purposes of
\f[CR]sendOrder\f[R] prioritization, or \f[CR]null\f[R] if they should
be part of the default group.
The default value is \f[CR]null\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]sendOrder\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
An integer value specifying the send priority of the returned
stream\(cqs datagrams.
Within the stream\(cqs \f[CR]sendGroup\f[R], bytes queued on
higher\-priority streams and datagrams are sent ahead of those from
lower\-priority ones.
The default value is \f[CR]0\f[R].
.RE
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]WebTransportDatagramsWritable\f[R] object, which extends
\f[CR]WritableStream\f[R].
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]InvalidStateError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if the transport\(cqs state is \f[CR]\(dqclosed\(dq\f[R] or
\f[CR]\(dqfailed\(dq\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]TypeError\f[R]
Thrown if \f[CR]sendGroup\f[R] is specified (non\-null) and is
associated with a different \f[CR]WebTransport\f[R].
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \f[B]\f[CB]createWritable()\f[B]\f[R] method is used to create a
\f[CR]WebTransportDatagramsWritable\f[R] instance for writing outgoing
datagrams.
.PP
The method allows you to specify a \f[CR]sendGroup\f[R] that defines the
group of streams and datagrams that this stream belongs to, and a
\f[CR]sendOrder\f[R] that sets the relative priority of this stream
within that group.
Within a group, bytes queued on higher\-priority streams and datagrams
are sent before any bytes from lower\-priority ones.
Different groups are expected to be treated as equals for the purposes
of bandwidth allocation \(em though the precise way bandwidth is divided
between groups is implementation\-defined.
.PP
The transmission is unreliable, meaning that even though you can define
the priority order, there is no guarantee that every datagram will be
sent, or that they will arrive in any particular order.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
This code shows how you can use the \f[CR]createWritable()\f[R] method
to get a \f[CR]WebTransportDatagramsWritable\f[R] and use it to send
data.
.PP
First we define a function to wrap our stream creation code.
This first constructs a \f[CR]WebTransport\f[R], and uses it with
\f[CR]createWritable()\f[R] to create a writable stream.
Note that because \f[CR]createWritable()\f[R] is not supported on all
browsers, the code falls back to the \f[CR]writable\f[R] property for
creating the writable.
.PP
\f[CR]getWriter()\f[R] is then called on \f[CR]writable\f[R] to create a
writer.
Because datagram delivery is unreliable, queued outgoing datagrams that
aren\(cqt sent in time are dropped.
For this reason, the code awaits the writer\(cqs \f[CR]ready\f[R]
promise before each write, so that datagrams are only written once the
underlying transport is ready to send them.
It also catches any errors from \f[CR]write()\f[R], since a rejection
means that a particular datagram was not sent.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]async\f[R] \f[B]function\f[R] sendDatagrams(url, datagrams, writableOptions = {}) {
  \f[B]const\f[R] wt = \f[B]new\f[R] WebTransport(url);
  \f[B]await\f[R] wt.ready;
  \f[B]const\f[R] writable =
    \f[B]typeof\f[R] wt.datagrams.createWritable === \(dqfunction\(dq
      ? wt.datagrams.createWritable(writableOptions)
      : wt.datagrams.writable;
  \f[B]const\f[R] writer = writable.getWriter();
  \f[B]for\f[R] (\f[B]const\f[R] bytes \f[B]of\f[R] datagrams) {
    \f[B]await\f[R] writer.ready;
    writer.write(bytes).catch(() \f[B]=>\f[R] {});
  }
}
.EE
.PP
This code shows how you might use the above method, passing a
\f[CR]sendOrder\f[R] of \f[CR]1\f[R] in the default send group:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] url = \(dqhttps://example.com/webtransport\(dq;
\f[B]const\f[R] datagrams = [\f[B]new\f[R] Uint8Array([65, 66, 67]), \f[B]new\f[R] Uint8Array([68, 69, 70])];
\f[B]await\f[R] sendDatagrams(url, datagrams, { sendOrder: 1 });
.EE
